+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Defect under sail
+
+The external browser acceptance suite fails on five TodoMVC behaviours: mark all complete, clear all complete, mark a todo complete, un-mark a todo complete, and edit a todo to empty text. The cause is one root defect: the list `render()` wipes and rebuilds every `<li>` on each item state change, so an element reference the browser holds across the click detaches from the document. The in-harness suite passed only because its steps re-query the DOM; the defect is hidden until a reference is held across the interaction.
+
+The fix is product intent, not a hint: item updates mutate the existing element in place (toggle class and checkbox state on the node that already exists) instead of rebuilding the list, and removing an item removes only that one node. `features/dom-identity.feature` pins this. The step definitions that record and re-assert element identity are verification support for QM to author.
+
+The in-harness happy-dom environment was confirmed to reproduce the node-identity loss with held references (the held `<li>` reports `isConnected: false` after the change), so each scenario in the watchbill reddens on the current code without needing a real browser.
