+Feature: Todo item DOM identity
+  As a person driving the app through a real browser
+  I want an item update to mutate that item's existing element in place
+  So that an element reference the browser holds across the interaction stays attached to the document
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo on preserves its list element
+    Given the app has the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | false     |
+    When the user records the current todo-list item elements
+    And the user clicks the toggle of the first todo item
+    Then the recorded todo-list item elements are still attached to the document
+    And the first recorded todo-list item element has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo off preserves its list element
+    Given the app has the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | true      |
+    When the user records the current todo-list item elements
+    And the user clicks the toggle of the first todo item
+    Then the recorded todo-list item elements are still attached to the document
+    And the first recorded todo-list item element does not have class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Marking all complete preserves every list element
+    Given the app has the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | false     |
+      | B     | false     |
+    When the user records the current todo-list item elements
+    And the user clicks "#toggle-all"
+    Then the recorded todo-list item elements are still attached to the document
+    And every recorded todo-list item element has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Clearing all complete preserves every list element
+    Given the app has the following todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | true      |
+      | B     | true      |
+    When the user records the current todo-list item elements
+    And the user clicks "#toggle-all"
+    Then the recorded todo-list item elements are still attached to the document
+    And no recorded todo-list item element has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Editing a todo to empty removes only that item and keeps its siblings
+    Given the app has the following todos:
+      | title     | completed |
+      | Remove me | false     |
+      | Keep me   | false     |
+    When the user records the current todo-list item elements
+    And the user double-clicks the label of the first todo item
+    And the user sets the edit input of the first todo item to "   "
+    And the user presses Enter in the edit input of the first todo item
+    Then ".todo-list" contains exactly 1 todo item
+    And the recorded todo-list item element at index 2 is still attached to the document
+    And the remaining todo item's label reads "Keep me"
